    {
      "id": "58808e53-d121-4d50-911b-b7753eaf86a7",
      "name": "Why MCP is Awesome - Part 1",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is Awesome - Part 1",
      "docTypeId": "aef7163d-bca4-4723-8b49-e151a40efe34",
      "templateId": "92df1916-8e03-43b9-8ebb-3285025c5176",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP is Awesome - Part 1"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-12 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "MCP provides a powerful way to interact with Umbraco through a standardized interface."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "listingImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4789-a1b2-c3d4e5f67890",
              "mediaKey": "52faafa0-ce10-4454-a852-47c5eddce889",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "c7e981ab-e4da-47f5-a4db-88d294e78de0",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "2649e282-8803-4f6d-9d7f-ec28553327c4",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "1f7eaa23-88b8-4842-9003-c150df8c690f",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "a06e95b0-8c96-48b8-b068-7b913edd498e",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "6772f1fd-3bd8-4117-9ea1-022445e4bbba",
                "key": "c7e981ab-e4da-47f5-a4db-88d294e78de0",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP (Model Context Protocol) is a revolutionary way to interact with applications like Umbraco. It provides a standardized interface that allows external tools and agents to perform operations without needing to understand the underlying implementation details.</p><p>In this first post, I'll explain the basics of MCP and why it's such a game-changer for content management systems.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "fd36e33b-e800-49ef-b034-8b6d53d06745",
                "key": "2649e282-8803-4f6d-9d7f-ec28553327c4",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "b2c3d4e5-f678-4901-a2b3-c4d5e6f78901",
                        "mediaKey": "8ec1066a-1448-498c-ae97-79ce6a161ddb",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Code on screen - the power of MCP"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "6772f1fd-3bd8-4117-9ea1-022445e4bbba",
                "key": "1f7eaa23-88b8-4842-9003-c150df8c690f",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>With MCP, you can perform complex operations through a simple, standardized interface. This means that tools like Claude Code can help you manage your Umbraco site without needing to understand the specifics of Umbraco's API.</p><p>The protocol abstracts away the complexity, making it easier to integrate with various systems.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "d5138491-02ee-4a51-a6b2-b46c8eacc03d",
                "key": "a06e95b0-8c96-48b8-b068-7b913edd498e",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "quote",
                    "value": "MCP is the future of application integration. It simplifies complex workflows and makes automation accessible to everyone."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "attribution",
                    "value": "— Tech Enthusiast"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "c7e981ab-e4da-47f5-a4db-88d294e78de0",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "2649e282-8803-4f6d-9d7f-ec28553327c4",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "1f7eaa23-88b8-4842-9003-c150df8c690f",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "a06e95b0-8c96-48b8-b068-7b913edd498e",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
